{
  "Short notifications at an edge of the window: four tones, an action such as Undo, a time of their own or none, six positions and a limit on how many show at once. Called programmatically; a region of your own can sit in JSX.": "",
  "Programmatic and declarative": "",
  "`toast.show()` and its tone shortcuts return the `Toast`, an object you can `close()`, `update()` or await. They use `Toaster.default`, made in `document.body` the first time; an app can put a `Toaster` of its own where it wants it in JSX and make it the default.": "",
  "`tone` sets the glyph, its color, and how a screen reader reads the toast: politely for `info` and `success`, at once for `caution` and `danger`.": "",
  "Action and Undo": "",
  "`action` adds a button; it runs `click`, then closes the toast. Make the undone thing come back, rather than asking first.": "",
  "Duration and update": "",
  "`duration` is 5 seconds by default; `0` keeps the toast until it is closed. Every option takes a function too, and `update()` changes a shown toast and starts its time again.": "",
  "Positions": "",
  "Six positions; start and end follow the reading direction. The newest toast is nearest the edge. A toast's `position` beats its toaster's.": "",
  "A toaster of your own, and max": "",
  "A `Toaster` is the region the toasts show in. `max` limits how many show at once at one position; the rest wait and come in as others close. This one sits right here in the page, so Tab reaches its toasts after these buttons.": "",
  "From anywhere on the page: to the newest toast. In a toast: back to where focus was.": "",
  "Through the toasts and their buttons. The default toaster is the last thing in the page, so Tab reaches it after the page content.": "",
  "With focus in a toast: closes it. Focus goes to the next toast, or back to where it came from.": "",
  "`<section role=\"region\">` named \"Notifications\" (`uiLocale`), with `aria-keyshortcuts` for the hotkey.": "",
  "Info and success toasts are read politely (`role=\"status\"`), caution and danger at once (`role=\"alert\"`). `update()` reads it again; a live `text` function does not, so a progress number is not read on every change.": "",
  "A toast never takes focus. Each toast is a group named by its title and text, and a Tab stop of its own, so one without buttons can be reached too.": "",
  "Timers stop while the pointer or focus is on the toasts and while the page is hidden (WCAG 2.2.1). Use `duration: 0` for anything the user must act on.": "",
  "It slides in and fades out with the motion tokens; with reduced motion it just appears.": "",
  "The name of the region and of the close button come from `uiLocale.strings` (`notifications`, `close`) and follow a change at once.": "",
  "The region.": "",
  "A stack at one position. `data-position`.": "",
  "A toast. `data-tone`, `data-state` (`entering`, `shown`, `leaving`).": "",
  "Its buttons (Buttons, `sm`).": "",
  "The width of a toast (never wider than the window).": "",
  "The distance to the window edge; how far it slides in from its edge (at a corner, also from its side).": "",
  "Where the action and close buttons sit across the toast.": "",
  "Units: the space between toasts; the toast with its box per tone (`success`, `caution`, `danger`) and under the keys (`focus`).": "",
  "Units a design may show: a stripe along the start edge, and a line that runs out with the time the toast stays; per tone.": "",
  "Units: the tone glyph and a plate behind it, per tone; the tone’s own mark.": "",
  "Units: the title, the message and the room around the buttons (their look is the `action` and `close` places’).": "",
  "Toast options and props": "",
  "The message.": "",
  "A bold line above it.": "",
  "`info`, `success`, `caution`, `danger`: the glyph, its color, and how a screen reader reads it.": "",
  "the tone glyph": "",
  "An icon of your own; `null` for none.": "",
  "Milliseconds it stays; `0` keeps it until it is closed.": "",
  "`{ text, click }`: a button in the toast, such as Undo. It runs `click(toast)`, then closes the toast.": "",
  "A close button, named from `uiLocale`.": "",
  "the toaster's": "",
  "Where it stacks: `top-start`, `top`, `top-end`, `bottom-start`, `bottom`, `bottom-end`.": "",
  "See the events.": "",
  "toast and Toast": "",
  "Shows a toast on `Toaster.default`.": "",
  "The same with the tone set.": "",
  "Closes every toast of `Toaster.default`.": "",
  "Closes it; a closed toast is disposed.": "",
  "Changes any of the options, starts its time again and reads it out again.": "",
  "Settles when it closes: `timeout`, `button`, `escape`, `action` or `code`.": "",
  "The same as an event.": "",
  "Every option is a property too, taking a value or a function.": "",
  "Toaster props": "",
  "Where its toasts stack unless a toast says otherwise.": "",
  "How many show at once at one position; the rest wait their turn.": "",
  "Moves focus to the newest toast, and back again; `''` for none.": "",
  "Timers stop while the pointer is over the toasts. They always stop while focus is in them or the page is hidden.": "",
